More than a year after KPop Demon Hunters became a global sensation &#x2014; a human-made antidote to the AI slop flooding the Internet &#x2014; billion-dollar hits like Toy Story 5 and The Super Mario Galaxy Movie and acclaimed work like Wildwood , Flow , Blue Eye Samurai , Arcane and X-Men '97 make the case that the human touch is still what moves animation audiences. Breaking in, though, has never been harder. The studio system is contracting, AI threatens to rewire production pipelines, and new platforms and producers (see: YouTube and Glitch) are redrawing the map. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Professional connections, fearless experimentation and creative innovation are key. Animation schools play a critical role, preparing emerging talent to be ready on day one to build upon existing pipelines of voices and projects that'll define the industry's next chapter. "The great thing about the industry is that because it's made up of artists, it's first and foremost a meritocracy," says Sam Goff, animation talent manager, recruiter and educator. "Networking and industry access also play a huge part, but you could have all the connections in the world, and if you don't have the skills and can't actually do the work, you're not getting hired." Related Stories Movies Hailee Steinfeld on Recording Music for New Movie 'Hexed' and Becoming a Mother in the Process Movies Magnolia Pictures Takes French Animated Gay Comedy 'Jim Queen' for U.S.

THR names the top U.S. schools where animation's next gen can do just that &#x2014; build their skills, professionally network and gain necessary industry access.

This program is about mastering teamwork and production so students can integrate seamlessly into 2D and 3D studio pipelines. Across its two colleges and three departments, Pixar, DreamWorks and Sony Animation veterans deliver a generalist approach that embraces arts and technology coursework while encouraging development in a single expertise. Professional development opportunities span internships at Disney Feature Animation and Lucas Arts/ILM, career and business strategy courses, and an annual student film created by the graduating class (2026's Dungeons & Dragons -inspired Love & Gold won a student Emmy). This year, a new arts building also added classrooms, computer labs, theaters, postproduction facilities and production stage access through a BYU Film collaboration.&#xA0; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

TUITION $7,096 (Church of Latter-Day Saints members); $14,192 (non-LDS members)

ALUMNI Jake Wyatt ( My Adventures With Superman )&#xA0;

The storied CalArts offers courses tied to animation history, theory, screenwriting, character design, sound and, yes, Disney movies, in classes that are small and taught entirely by working artists. The Patty Disney Center for Life and Work uses a mix of support &#x2014; one-on-one career advising, an entrepreneurial incubator program, a career and opportunity festival, animation portfolio day, weekly guest speakers and a robust internship program. The approach has produced talent like experimental animator and Oscar nominee Siqi Song ( Sister ) and Lindsay Scanlan, whose fourth-year film went viral before she was hired for the Disney Channel series The Ghost and Molly McGee .

ALUMNI Sean Buckelew ( Common Side Effects ); Glen Keane ( The Little Mermaid )

Boasting 13 scholarships, the School of Art's diverse and industry-adjacent program is an affordable option for learning animated filmmaking or preproduction. Led by faculty who've worked on King of the Hill and at Disneyland Paris, students are exposed to studio art and a breadth of animation forms alongside internships at studios like Titmouse and Bento Box, with recent graduates hired at MrBeast and HBO. This year, students will produce an animated short in collaboration with the U.N., and a new animation incubator &#x2014; launched in partnership with ASIFA-Hollywood &#x2014; will bring alums and other industry talent to campus, offering students mentorship and production opportunities on innovative shorts tackling social activism and cutting-edge technologies.&#xA0; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

TUITION $3,419 (in-state); $10,017 (out-of-state)

ALUMNI Daniel Chong ( Hoppers ); Theresa Reyes ( Toy Story 4 )&#xA0;

DePaul's breadth of concentrations are taught by a large, full-time faculty, with access to animators in residence like Brian Ferguson ( The Lion King , Mulan ). Student orgs connect with Chicago's animation community, and there are practical courses, such as one co-created and run by Nickelodeon Animation directors that taught the studio's process for storyboarding the show SpongeBob SquarePants . An L.A.-focused internship program brings DePaul to Hollywood, with work at ShadowMachine and the Jim Henson Co. This year, the school expanded the capabilities of its virtual production LED Volume with enhanced motion-capture systems, introduced an animation cohort to its six-week summer Chicago Housing Authority program, and offered new career development opportunities with visual effects company DNEG and through a Film + Animation Industry Night.&#xA0;

TUITION $48,180 (undergraduate); $1,003 per credit hour (graduate)

ALUMNI Molly McCandless ( Wildwood ), Sebastian Newell (Nickelodeon + CBS Animation Studios)

Those with a strong portfolio, unique personal perspective and penchant for experimentation will find a home in the Illustration and Film/Animation/Video (FAV) program, which boasts a more than 90 percent freshman retention and school graduation rate despite its famously intensive coursework. Graduates of RISD's animation-related undergraduate and graduate degrees, which combine arts and liberal arts studies, frequently leave their mark as independent entrepreneurs or in studio work like directing, writing, animating, character designing and producing at such companies as Pixar, DreamWorks, HBO and PBS. This year, FAV's course catalog expanded to include production design, live-action puppetry and other multidisciplinary, design-driven courses, while the school hosted the inaugural symposium for its recently launched Movement Lab in October.&#xA0; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

ALUMNI Michaela Olsen and Emily Collins (Mighty Oak studio)

Alongside alumni speakers like Diane Ikemiyashiro, a vp at Disney Junior, and Hotel Transylvania 5 co-director Alan Hawkins, students are educated by faculty with credits on Avatar: Fire and Ash and Stranger Things: Tales From '85 in a rigorous curriculum spanning foundational art and the animation pipeline. A pre-college program unlocks access to financial aid before enrolling, while current students and recent alums have secured internships or work at Pixar, DreamWorks, Sony and Netflix Animation. Its new 2D Character Animation B.F.A. will also help students develop the artistic, technical and entrepreneurial foundation needed for today's evolving animation industry, whether working at a major studio, in a freelance career or launching a creator-owned indie production.

ALUMNI Michael Yates ( Incredibles 3 ); Michelle Cowart ( Forgotten Island )

For a cutting-edge institution offering the latest animation tools and techniques with a well-connected alumni network, look to SCAD's School of Animation and Motion or collaborative programs in interactive design and game development, themed entertainment design and illustration at the Savannah and Atlanta campuses. In the past five years, students have participated in screenings and master classes, been hired at Laika and Sony Pictures Imageworks, and interned at Disney Imagineering and Steamroller Animation. Alongside alumni working on three of 2026's best animation Oscar nominees, student animated films have earned more than 400 official selections and recognitions, including the Student Academy Awards, College Television Awards and Cannes Indie Shorts Awards.&#xA0; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

TUITION $42,975 (undergraduate); $43,965 (graduate)

ALUMNI Zach Parrish ( The Sea Beast ); Vinod Krishnan ( The Simpsons )

Emerging artists &#x2014; including Pell-qualifying graduates of New York City high schools awarded a minimum $30,000 annually as incoming freshmen &#x2014; can access undergrad and grad programs that support the mastery of the entire 3D and VFX pipeline, foundational art, animation history, specialization training and short-film production. Its classes hone students' animation, motion design or experimental art visions. Students have access to state-of-the-art and industry-standard software and gear, as well as labs supporting sound, motion-capture, stop-motion and pencil work. That's alongside a pre-college program; the SVA in L.A. networking program; studio visits to Walt Disney Animation; portfolio reviews by Pixar and Skydance employees; lectures and workshops with WIA, VES, SIGGRAPH and ASIFA; a senior industry networking mixer; and career courses, including pilot writing and pitching techniques.&#xA0;

TUITION $27,635 (undergraduate); $30,845 (graduate)

ALUMNI Vivienne Medrano ( Hazbin Hotel ); Enrico Casarosa ( Luca )

With a 5-to-1 student-to-teacher ratio, access to live-action electives and funding support like the Matt Groening Production Fellowship in Animation, the school's M.F.A. via the Animation Workshop offers a distinctly intimate pathway to learning every phase of filmmaking through the lens of animation. At the school, founded in 1948 by former Disney animator Bill Shull, students complete three films while learning from artists like Phoebe & Jay co-creator Thy Than and interning at studios like Starburns Industries. This year, they also heard from alums on DreamWorks Animation's Forgotten Island and benefited from the addition of four full-body and facial motion-capture systems and an eMotimo Spectrum ST4 to support student work in stop-motion.&#xA0; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid5' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

TUITION $13,722 (in-state); $25,967 (out-of-state)

ALUMNI Latoya Raveneau ( The Proud Family: Louder and Prouder )

What do Hexed , Shrek 5 , The Cat in the Hat and GOAT have in common? All four have USC faculty on their crews. With working artists running the classes, the curriculum keeps pace with the industry, with a focus on creation, design, innovation and cross-industry collaboration. Alongside efforts like Studio Day, which attracts 20-plus companies for interviews and portfolio reviews, faculty walk students through the applications, interviews and contract negotiations. The programs' success is evidenced by 2025 graduates like Pablo Diaz De Leon Hicks and Matthew Sorgie, both selected for the 2026 American Pavilion Emerging Filmmaker Showcase at Cannes.

TUITION $75,384 (undergraduate); $61,299 (graduate)

ALUMNI Andrew Millstein (Annapurna Animation); Lori Forte ( Ice Age )

9 OTHER SCHOOLS TO WATCH THANKS TO DISTINCT OPPORTUNITIES AND PARTNERSHIPS

When Amy Hurwitz, a veteran of LAIKA's recruitment team, reached out to Bowie State University about a potential partnership around the start of the pandemic, Tewodross Melchishua Williams, professor, program and internship coordinator for the school&#x2019;s Department of Fine and Performing Arts, was &#x201C;immediately excited about what that could mean for our students,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;HBCUs have extraordinary talent, but we don't always have the same access to specialized facilities, equipment, funding, or direct industry relationships as other institutions.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid6' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The partnership with the Oregon-based studio helps close some of those gaps, offering the students in Visual Communication and Digital Media Arts (VCDMA) access to Bowie&#x2019;s first stop-motion course. Through it, around 20 students annually learn sculpture, cinematography, fabrication, and storytelling alongside character and puppet design, set construction and lighting, frame-by-frame animation, and post-production.

The school is also now home to Studio Ayoka Chenzira, funded by LAIKA and named in honor of Dr. Ayoka Chenzira, a pioneering filmmaker, animator, and department chair at Spelman College. &#x201C;For me, that name matters,&#x201D; says Williams. &#x201C;It connects the space to an African American woman whose work helped expand what animation and experimental filmmaking could be, and it gives our students a legacy to learn from.&#x201D;

Both initiatives have unlocked access to industry professionals, professional workflows, summer intensive workshops, and internship opportunities, with this year&#x2019;s LAIKA movie Wildwood counting three very recent alumni as either crew or interns. &#x201C;I tell students that talent matters, but so does curiosity, discipline, collaboration, and professionalism,&#x201D; the Bowie State professor says. &#x201C;Seeing our alumni contribute to a feature like Wildwood makes those lessons tangible.&#x201D;

For LAIKA, the partnership has resulted in more facilities and access to &#x201C;talented emerging artists whose backgrounds and perspectives can broaden the field,&#x201D; says Williams. &#x201C;The industry needs technical skill, absolutely, but it also needs more voices and different perspectives.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid7' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The collaboration has also inspired similar efforts, like a partnership between Gobelins Paris, Netflix, and Guillermo del Toro, with the support of animation studio ShadowMachine. These serve as &#x201C;a powerful reminder of the artistry, patience, and human craftsmanship at the heart of animation&#x201D; in the age of AI, notes Williams. &#x201C;For students, that's an important lesson: even as technology changes, foundational skills in movement, design, lighting, storytelling, and collaboration remain essential.&#x201D;

Below, THR looks at other schools with distinct parnterships and opportunities.

Creative Network: At Loyola Marymount University, faculty member Sydney Bright, head of global animation at WEBTOON Productions, leads a Studio Development Series for animated content. At NYU, home to The Jeff Baena Award, an undergraduate production scholarship supporting advanced-level projects, Nickelodeon&#x2019;s senior vice president, TV series animation, Claudi Spinelli serves as one of the Animation Alumni Association&#x2019;s founding members.

Gamers Gateway: Rochester Institute of Technology is home to Magic Spell Studios, out of which the student-run Overshoot Animation Productions supports the development of indie games, films and animated series. And Texas A&M&#x2019;s programs support research in game-based learning and direct partnerships with studios like ProbablyMonsters at the Fort Worth Visualization campus.

Local Connections : Through Kansas City Art Institute&#x2019;s Sponsored Studio program, animation students created a 22-episode series for the Kansas City Royals Dominican Academy. At Massachusetts College of Art and Design, emerging animators can team with students at the Berklee College of Music to help their projects receive top level musical scores. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid8' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Universe Building: The B.F.A.&#x2019;s story emphasis offers specialization specifically in animation story development while the Otis x Pixar Story Workshop lets selected students experience a studio-level story development process. The University of Central Florida&#x2019;s Emerging Media B.F.A. Animation and Visualization track develops storytelling and animation skills around themed entertainment, with numerous professional development opportunities via the UCF/Universal Creative Lab partnership.

